description=AMD FidelityFX (FSR) upscaling for Project Zomboid B42, one mod with two loading modes: EITHER add -javaagent pointing at this mod's media\java\fsr-upsc-agent.jar to the launch options (load-time agent, no extra mod needed), OR just keep ZombieBuddy (release 2.x or BETA 3.x) installed and enable this mod - ZombieBuddy loads the same jar from mod.info and retransforms the game in place (first launch shows the ZombieBuddy approval dialog, choose persist). World pass renders at a reduced resolution (FidelityFX quality presets) and is resolved with FSR 1 EASU+RCAS, or FSR 2 / FSR 3.1 temporal upscaling (GL compute) with injected sub-pixel camera jitter, depth chain, auto-reactive masks and entity motion vectors, plus optional software frame generation on the present path (FsrControl.fsr2FgTest). Falls back to FSR 1 automatically on any compute fault. Running both modes at once is safe: the second entry detects the armed JVM and stands down. Built for B42.22 (revision e013dbb529) only: the mod list version gate (versionMin/versionMax) blocks enabling on other builds, and a same-label hotfix would run stock instead of transforming.

The agent jar ships inside this mod folder: media\java\fsr-upsc-agent.jar.
In the ZombieBuddy mode it is loaded from mod.info (javaJarFile/javaPkgName)
on game start; in the javaagent mode point the launch option at the same file.
Hook groups, downscale and upscaler settings behave identically in both modes
(ModOptions.ini / fsrupsc.FsrControl from Lua).
